## Interface:
- Inputs: tankLevel (REAL), outletFlow (REAL), inletPermit (BOOL), resetBtn (BOOL)
- Outputs: pumpRun (BOOL), alarmHigh (BOOL), alarmLow (BOOL), outletValveOpen (BOOL)

## Key behaviors:
1. High level alarm (alarmHigh): latches when tankLevel >= 85.0, cleared only by resetBtn rising edge when condition is safe (tankLevel < 85.0)
2. Low level alarm (alarmLow): latches when tankLevel <= 15.0, cleared only by resetBtn rising edge when condition is safe (tankLevel > 15.0)
3. Reset button rising edge is required to clear alarms - holding across level changes doesn't trigger new reset
4. First scan: button is treated as FALSE
5. pumpRun = TRUE only when inletPermit=TRUE AND no alarms active
6. outletValveOpen = FALSE when alarmLow is active, TRUE otherwise

## Formal properties:
- S1: G(tankLevel >= 85.0 -> alarmHigh) - high level always triggers alarm
- S2: G(alarmHigh & !X(rising(resetBtn)) -> X(alarmHigh)) - alarm latches
- S3: G(alarmHigh -> !pumpRun) - alarm stops pump
- S4: G(tankLevel <= 15.0 -> !outletValveOpen) - low level closes valve
- S5: G(!inletPermit -> !pumpRun) - no permit = no pump
- N10-S2: G(tankLevel < 85.0 -> (alarmHigh <-> (prev(alarmHigh) AND !rising(resetBtn)))) - alarm persists without reset edge


- N10-S3: G((alarmHigh OR alarmLow) -> !pumpRun) - either alarm disables pump
- N10-S4: G(outletValveOpen <-> !alarmLow) - valve state inverts with low alarm
- N10-S5: G((!alarmHigh AND !alarmLow) -> (pumpRun <-> inletPermit)) - pump follows permit when no alarms
- N10-S6: G(alarmLow <-> ((tankLevel <= 15.0) OR (prev(alarmLow) AND !rising(resetBtn)))) - low alarm latches and requires reset

